<header>
<h1 class="p-name">Playstation 5 | First Impressions &amp; My Opinion | PS5</h1>
</header>
<section data-field="subtitle" class="p-summary">
PLAYSTATION 5 | FIRST IMPRESSIONS &amp; MY OPINION | PS5
</section>
<section data-field="body" class="e-content">
<section name="2781" class="section section--body section--first"><div class="section-divider"><hr class="section-divider"></div><div class="section-content"><div class="section-inner sectionLayout--insetColumn"><h3 name="ff51" id="ff51" class="graf graf--h3 graf--leading graf--title">Playstation 5 | First Impressions &amp; My Opinion | PS5</h3><p name="ba9f" id="ba9f" class="graf graf--p graf-after--h3"><strong class="markup--strong markup--p-strong">PLAYSTATION 5 | FIRST IMPRESSIONS &amp; MY OPINION | PS5</strong></p><figure name="b3d2" id="b3d2" class="graf graf--figure graf-after--p"><img class="graf-image" data-image-id="0*PbT74cTOl-KxbtSo.png" data-width="1080" data-height="510" data-is-featured="true" src="https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/800/0*PbT74cTOl-KxbtSo.png"></figure><p name="67bb" id="67bb" class="graf graf--p graf-after--figure">The PlayStation has been the most successful line up for Sony. The original PlayStation which was launched in 1994 was the first video game console to sell 100 million units. The PlayStation remains undefeated in the gaming industry. Each and every generation is more advanced than the previous generation. It is a game changer in the gaming industry.</p><p name="645a" id="645a" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">And now, Sony has officially introduced the PS5. The graphics were stunning and the gameplay was real smooth in the trailer shown. I think gaming will be an immersive experience in the PS5.</p><figure name="63aa" id="63aa" class="graf graf--figure graf-after--p"><img class="graf-image" data-image-id="0*s848iaOM-iq_GHNZ.png" data-width="800" data-height="450" src="https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/800/0*s848iaOM-iq_GHNZ.png"></figure><p name="59e5" id="59e5" class="graf graf--p graf-after--figure">I am eagerly waiting to play Spider-Man: Miles Morales in the PS5. Do let me know, what is your favorite video game in the comments.</p><figure name="01f4" id="01f4" class="graf graf--figure graf-after--p"><img class="graf-image" data-image-id="0*PfjSp-wf-5BGFLha.png" data-width="1088" data-height="612" src="https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/800/0*PfjSp-wf-5BGFLha.png"></figure><p name="37e7" id="37e7" class="graf graf--p graf-after--figure">The design of the PS5 is futuristic. The black &amp; white combination is fantastic unlike the PS4’s design. Sony has done a great job. The regular edition and the digital edition look quite similar except the regular one has an optical drive and the digital edition doesn’t.</p><p name="a1bd" id="a1bd" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Now, you may be wondering, why there is a digital edition? Back in the day, many people did not have an excellent internet connection. They had a connection only good enough to surf the net. They couldn’t download games that are like 100 GB. The only way to play a game for them is to buy a disk from a retail store.</p><p name="3aeb" id="3aeb" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">But now things have changed. Most people have an excellent internet connection. They can buy games from online websites like steam and store it in the cloud and use it whenever necessary. The digital edition is the go-to option for most people. On my opinion, the digital edition is gonna be a huge success.</p><p name="3632" id="3632" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p"><strong class="markup--strong markup--p-strong">The Controller:</strong></p><figure name="842d" id="842d" class="graf graf--figure graf-after--p"><img class="graf-image" data-image-id="0*f0eFwW01pikYnNau.png" data-width="893" data-height="441" src="https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/800/0*f0eFwW01pikYnNau.png"></figure><p name="0c66" id="0c66" class="graf graf--p graf-after--figure">The controller is getting more and more advanced. They have upgraded their dual shock controller from the previous generation to a dual sense controller. As the name suggests, Sony has adopted haptic feedback in the controller and also in the L2 R2 buttons. This controller gives us a sensation like shooting a real gun and driving a car through mud.</p><p name="f4e4" id="f4e4" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">The new controller also has an in-built microphone, so that gamers can chat easily without a headset.</p><p name="e9d3" id="e9d3" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p"><strong class="markup--strong markup--p-strong">Technical specifications:</strong></p><p name="9331" id="9331" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">CPU : AMD Zen 2-based CPU with 8 cores at 3.5GHz (variable frequency).</p><p name="d5e7" id="d5e7" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">GPU : 10.28 TFLOPs, 36 CUs at 2.23 GHZ (variable frequency).</p><p name="e1c6" id="e1c6" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">GPU architecture : Custom RDNA 2.</p><p name="52f8" id="52f8" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Memory interface : 16GB GDDR6/256-bit.</p><p name="5f5a" id="5f5a" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Memory bandwidth : 448 GB/S</p><p name="001b" id="001b" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Internal storage : Custom 825GB SSD.</p><p name="1d0b" id="1d0b" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">IO throughput : 5.5GB/S (raw), typical 8–9 GB/S (compressed).</p><p name="e444" id="e444" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Expandable storage : NVMe SSD slot.</p><p name="89e5" id="89e5" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">External storage : USB HDD support(PS4 games only).</p><p name="2ff7" id="2ff7" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Optical drive : 4K UHD Blu-ray drive.</p><p name="cb8b" id="cb8b" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Sony hasn’t officially released the price of the PS5. But according to leaks, it is expected to be priced around 450 USD (34000 INR) for the regular edition and 400 USD(30500 INR) for the digital edition, which is awesome.</p><p name="cb1a" id="cb1a" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p"><strong class="markup--strong markup--p-strong">My opinion:</strong></p><p name="0a36" id="0a36" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">I think the digital edition is going to be a huge success because of the affordable pricing. The PS5 also has backward compatibility, so that if you have PS4 games, you can run them in PS5.</p><p name="e291" id="e291" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">When it comes to VR compatibility, there is no official confirmation for the native games. But as the console supports backward compatibility, which will naturally include PS VR games as well. If you are a gamer, then you are in for a real treat. If they bring the PS5 around 450 USD, it would be awesome.</p><p name="d0dd" id="d0dd" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Do let me know, which is your favorite video game in the comments section.👍</p><p name="7976" id="7976" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p">Have fun gaming!😎😎</p><p name="35a4" id="35a4" class="graf graf--p graf-after--p graf--trailing"><strong class="markup--strong markup--p-strong">P.S</strong> : If you share this, it would make my day😉</p></div></div></section><section name="26f0" class="section section--body section--last"><div class="section-divider"><hr class="section-divider"></div><div class="section-content"><div class="section-inner sectionLayout--insetColumn"><p name="6e33" id="6e33" class="graf graf--p graf--leading graf--trailing"><em class="markup--em markup--p-em">Originally published at </em><a href="https://thetechnobyte.blogspot.com/2020/06/playstation-5-first-impression-my.html" data-href="https://thetechnobyte.blogspot.com/2020/06/playstation-5-first-impression-my.html" class="markup--anchor markup--p-anchor" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><em class="markup--em markup--p-em">https://thetechnobyte.blogspot.com</em></a><em class="markup--em markup--p-em"> on June 30, 2020.</em></p></div></div></section>
</section>
<footer><p>By <a href="https://medium.com/@gokulrece23" class="p-author h-card">Gokul Rajan</a> on <a href="https://medium.com/p/29d71bce240e"><time class="dt-published" datetime="2020-06-30T10:07:07.591Z">June 30, 2020</time></a>.</p><p><a href="https://medium.com/@gokulrece23/playstation-5-first-impressions-my-opinion-ps5-29d71bce240e" class="p-canonical">Canonical link</a></p><p>Exported from <a href="https://medium.com">Medium</a> on April 28, 2026.</p></footer></article></body></html>